# Plan: pkg/cmux — cmux integration package

## Context

The user wants a reusable `pkg/cmux` package that wraps the cmux CLI (exec-based, `CMUX_WORKSPACE_ID` detection) so any module in the app can call `cmux.Notify(ctx, title, body)` after finishing work — the same way `pkg/notify` is used today but focused purely on cmux. The existing `pkg/notify` / `modules/notify` stay untouched; this is a new lightweight peer package.

Use-case anchor: `modules/dotfiles` — when `runSync` finishes, it calls `cmux.Notify(ctx, "Dotfiles", "Sync complete")` if cmux is available.

## Approach

1. Add `pkg/cmux/` — a thin client package with an `Available()` check and typed methods that exec the `cmux` CLI.
2. Wire one concrete usage into `modules/dotfiles` as the reference example.
3. No new CLI command, no changes to `modules/notify`, no config required.

The package surface:

```go
// Available returns true when CMUX_WORKSPACE_ID is set
func Available() bool

// Notify sends a desktop notification via `cmux notify --title … --body …`
func Notify(ctx context.Context, title, body string) error

// SetStatus sets a sidebar status key via `cmux set-status <key> <value> [--icon …] [--color …]`
func SetStatus(ctx context.Context, key, value string, opts ...StatusOpt) error

// ClearStatus clears a sidebar status key
func ClearStatus(ctx context.Context, key string) error
```

`StatusOpt` options: `WithIcon(name string)`, `WithColor(hex string)`.

Only the functions actually needed by dotfiles (and future callers) are added — start with `Available()` and `Notify()`.

